  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Thursday)\nIssued at 102 PM CDT Fri Sep 18 2026\n\nMorning upper air maps show a 596 - 598 dm ridge over the Mid-\nSouth. Strong diurnal heating underneath the ridge will bring a\ncontinuation of near-record temperatures across the region with\nhighs likely reaching the upper 90s and low 100s through this\nafternoon. Dewpoint observations show values in the middle to\nupper 60s, which are expected to mix down slightly through this\nevening, but values should remain high enough to allow for heat\nindices above 105 F. Model guidance is still in good agreement\nthat the ridge will continue to sit over the region into this\nweekend, although slowly weakening in amplitude. Therefore,\ntemperatures around 100 F are expected through Saturday\nafternoon, potentially as far out as Sunday, with similar heat\nindex values to today. In turn, a Heat Advisory is in effect\nareawide through Saturday evening at 8 PM CDT. Just enough\nuncertainty remains regarding heat index values Sunday afternoon\nto preclude the extension of the Heat Advisory through Sunday.\n\nMedium range guidance continues to trend towards higher\nconfidence in a further weakening of the upper ridge into the\nearly part of next week. The primary drivers for this weakening\nare from two troughs, one across the northern Plains and another\nover the Gulf, that act in tandem to smooth out the ridge. By\nMonday afternoon, 500 mb heights will be potentially as low as\n586 dm, leading to a drastic change in low-level temperatures. At\nthe same time, a 1030+ mb surface high will develop across\neastern Canada and the northeastern CONUS, pushing cooler air\nsouthwestward across the Great Lakes and Atlantic Coastline\nthrough midweek.\n\nThe rest of the forecast period will then likely be dominated by\nsurface high pressure as northwesterlies replace the ridging and \nsurface northerlies keep drier air locked into the region. \nFurthermore, cooler surface theta e and upper subsidence will keep\nPoPs below mentionable through the end of next week. Expect daily\nhighs in the middle to upper 80s Wednesday and beyond with lows \nin the low to middle 60s. Although we may have been burned, both \nliterally and figuratively by the temperature forecast in the past\nweek and a half, guidance has certainly started to converge on \nthis cooler solution. So, look forward to more bearable heat on \nthe horizon.",
